{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLAUDE.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:26:47.273860Z","id":"b4bf9bfe4d2ea4a80cf12f79b3f0b39b39b49e81ccaa0eb3fe9f80e29049f0fd","body":{"detail":"CLAUDE.md:242 reads '`--project-under <dir>` (on both `p cache sync` and `path query`) restricts to sessions whose project directory is under that subtree', while `ShareArgs.project_under` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:72) adds the flag to `share --all` and CLAUDE.md:102 shows it in use. The same bullet's note that Claude compares in slug space applies to pi as well (`pi_project_in_scope`, crates/path-cli/src/sync/sources.rs:475), which matters more now that the flag drives an upload. Separately, the share bullet at CLAUDE.md:227 says sessions 'are stamped with one `enumerate` pass per harness, not a per-session stat', but `row_stamp` (cmd_share.rs:999-1012) falls back to `source_stamp` — a per-session stat, and for codex/gemini a full listing — for any row the enumeration did not surface.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":242},"end":{"line":242},"content_hash":"35dc2e0cd24df58bab5219b7428c898dc625be737c91f33ea3a028daa981781c"},"suggested_fix":"Amend CLAUDE.md:242 to list `share --all` alongside `p cache sync` and `path query` and to name pi with claude in the slug-space note; in the share bullet say 'one `enumerate` pass per harness, with a per-session stat only for rows the enumeration did not list'.","summary":"CLAUDE.md's `--project-under` bullet still says the flag is on `p cache sync` and `path query` only; `share --all` now takes it, and the share bullet's 'not a per-session stat' overstates `enumerate_stamps`","tags":["review","review:pr-355-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"CLAUDE.md","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:32:55.040820Z","id":"aac68ff8a032ae35fe59594c5b07123642bd01055955f92a37dc77bc238f58b4","body":{"detail":"CLAUDE.md:242 reads '`--project-under <dir>` (on both `p cache sync` and `path query`)'. `ShareArgs.project_under` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:71-72, `#[arg(long, requires = \"all\", value_name = \"DIR\")]`) adds the flag to `share --all`, and CLAUDE.md:102 itself shows `share --all --project-under ~/work`. The same bullet attributes slug-space comparison to Claude only, but `project_in_scope` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/sources.rs:97-103) routes `ArtifactType::Pi` to `pi_project_in_scope` (sources.rs:475-486), which also compares in encoded space. CLAUDE.md:227 says 'Sessions are stamped with one `enumerate` pass per harness, not a per-session stat', but `row_stamp` (cmd_share.rs:999-1012) does `.unwrap_or_else(|| source_stamp(bundle, row.artifact_type, row_project(row), &row.session_id))` for any row the enumeration did not surface, and `enumerate_stamps`'s own doc comment (cmd_share.rs:969-972) notes the per-session `stamp` lookup is a full listing for most providers. Documentation drift; `suggestion` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"b4bf9bfe4d2ea4a80cf12f79b3f0b39b39b49e81ccaa0eb3fe9f80e29049f0fd","summary":"confirmed: CLAUDE.md:242 omits share --all from the --project-under flag list, and :227's 'not a per-session stat' overstates row_stamp, which falls back to source_stamp","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
